assistant: Subject: follow next_cursor to fetch all search result pages

In vendor version 2026-10-01, `GET /products` started splitting results into pages (5 of 7 items, `next_cursor: "5"`), using the `cursor` parameter and `next_cursor` field that were already in the spec. `search_products` only read the first page, so it returned 5 items while reporting `total: 7`. It now keeps requesting `&cursor=<next_cursor>` and combines the items until `next_cursor` is null. The old 2026-01-01 version always returns `next_cursor: null`, so it still sends one request and gives the same output. Typecheck, lint and the other tests pass; the repro test now fails with the expected UNMATCHED_REQUEST for `GET /products?q=cable&cursor=5` until it is re-recorded. Separately, I haven't fixed a second problem: the 2026-10-01 recording returns prices about 100× higher than the old version (6900 vs 69), probably in cents. The tool passes them through as US dollars, so they will break the `items.price.range` rule (20–2000 USD) once the call is re-recorded.

